  "Question": "When the repeating decimal \\(0.363636\\ldots\\) is written in simplest fractional form, the sum of the numerator and denominator is:",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(15\\)",
    "B": "\\(45\\)",
    "C": "\\(114\\)",
    "D": "\\(135\\)",
    "E": "\\(150\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "A",
  "Solution": "The repeating block has two digits, so multiplying by \\(100\\) makes the decimal tails line up. Let \\(t=0.363636\\ldots\\). Then\n\\[\n100t=36.363636\\ldots=36+t.\n\\]\nSubtracting \\(t\\) gives \\(99t=36\\), so\n\\[\nt=\\frac{36}{99}=\\frac{4}{11},\n\\]\nwhere we divided the numerator and denominator by \\(9\\). Since \\(4\\) and \\(11\\) have no common factor greater than \\(1\\), this fraction is in simplest form. The requested sum is \\(4+11=15\\), choice \\(\\mathrm{A}\\).",
